c-2101-5081-94d4-70ba5b197dd1" 13194139534687 true] [17592186303411 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5 & =7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{(x+5)}^{2}}{49} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-13 & =7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(y-13)^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{(y-13)}^{2}}{49} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{(x+5)}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{(y-13)}^{2}}{49} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{(x+5)}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{(y-13)}^{2}}{49} & =1 \\\\ {(x+5)}^{2}+{(y-13)}^{2} & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation is ${(x+5)}^{2}+{(y-13)}^{2}=49.$" 13194139534687 true] [17592186303412 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303413 13194139534687 true] [17592186303412 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534687 true] [17592186303412 1041 "field-1" 13194139534687 true] [17592186303412 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303413 13194139534687 true] [17592186303412 1110 #uuid "9afcc869-c49f-52fb-8874-10c9e350a7dd" 13194139534687 true] [17592186303413 1034 "5" 13194139534687 true] [17592186303413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534687 true] [17592186303413 1111 #uuid "37511343-3a89-56ab-b839-1525b4ea9ee0" 13194139534687 true] [17592186303414 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303415 13194139534687 true] [17592186303414 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534687 true] [17592186303414 1041 "field-2" 13194139534687 true] [17592186303414 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303415 13194139534687 true] [17592186303414 11